  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Who?",
   "texto": [
    "**谁** means «who». **哪位** asks «which person» courteously. **这位** is «this person» and **那位**, «that person». The qualifier - the \"\" - goes between the demonstrative and the person."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Relationship and gender",
   "texto": [
    "**先生** equals «Sir.» and **女士**, «Madam.» or «Miss». **同学** is a classmate; **同事** is a working partner. These words do not have a gender mark.",
    "**也** means «too» and **都**, «All». In mandarin, both are usually placed before the verb."
   ]
  },
